```c
#include <openssl/srtm.h>

void ossl_quic_srtm_free(QUIC_SRTM *srtm)
{
    if (srtm == NULL)
        return;

    SRTM_ITEM *item = srtm->items;
    while (item != NULL)
    {
        SRTM_ITEM *next = item->next;
        OPENSSL_free(item);
        item = next;
    }

    OPENSSL_free(srtm);
}
```
This function takes a pointer to a `QUIC_SRTM` structure as input, and frees all the memory associated with it. It does this by iterating over the `items` field of the `QUIC_SRTM` structure, and freeing each item in turn using the `OPENSSL_free` function. Finally, it frees the `QUIC_SRTM` structure itself using the `OPENSSL_free` function.

Note that this function assumes that the `items` field of the `QUIC_SRTM` structure is a linked list of `SRTM_ITEM` structures, and that each `SRTM_ITEM` structure has a `next` field that points to the next item in the list. If this is not the case, the function will need to be modified accordingly.

