Here is an example of a function in C programming language that checks if a Redis command has a push as a reply:
```
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int cmdHasPushAsReply(struct redisCommand *cmd) {
    if (cmd == NULL) {
        return 0;
    }

    // Check if the command is a subscribe or unsubscribe command
    if (strcmp(cmd->name, "subscribe") == 0 || strcmp(cmd->name, "unsubscribe") == 0) {
        // Check if the command has a push as a reply
        if (cmd->flags & REDIS_CMD_PUSH_AS_REPLY) {
            return 1;
        }
    }

    return 0;
}
```
This function takes a `struct redisCommand` pointer as an argument and checks if the command has a push as a reply. If the command is a subscribe or unsubscribe command and has a push as a reply, the function returns `1`. Otherwise, it returns `0`.

You can use this function to check if a Redis command has a push as a reply before executing it. For example:
```
