Value *llvm::createAnyOfOp(IRBuilderBase &Builder, Value *StartVal, RecurKind RK, Value *Left, Value *Right) {
    // Create a new value of the same type as StartVal
    Value *NewVal = Builder.CreateValue(StartVal->getType());

    // Create a new PHI node with the same type as StartVal
    PHINode *PHI = Builder.CreatePHI(StartVal->getType(), 2);

    // Add the initial start value to the PHI node
    PHI->addIncoming(StartVal, Builder.GetInsertBlock());

    // Add the loop invariant value to the PHI node
    PHI->addIncoming(Right, Builder.GetInsertBlock());

    // Create a new select instruction with the PHI node as the condition
    SelectInst *Select = Builder.CreateSelect(PHI, Left, Right);

    // Set the recurrence kind of the select instruction
    Select->setRecurrenceKind(RK);

    // Return the new value
    return NewVal;
}
```
This function creates a new value of the same type as the initial start value, and then creates a new PHI node with two incoming values: the initial start value and the loop invariant value. It then creates a new select instruction with the PHI node as the condition, and sets the recurrence kind of the select instruction to the given recurrence kind. Finally, it returns the new value.

Note that this function assumes that the initial start value and the loop invariant value are of the same type, and that the recurrence kind is valid. It also assumes that the IRBuilderBase object has a valid insert block.

