The `Width` parameter is used to determine the number of bits per hex number. It is used to determine when to print a space between hex numbers.

Note that this function assumes that the `BitVector` is little-endian, meaning that the least significant bit is stored in the first element of the `BitVector`. If the `BitVector` is big-endian, the function will need to be modified accordingly.

