If the `BT_USE_SSE_IN_API` and `BT_USE_SSE` macros are not defined, it checks if the `BT_USE_NEON` macro is defined. If it is, it uses the NEON instruction set to perform the division. It divides the vector by the scalar value using the `vdivq_n_f32` instruction.

If neither of the above macros are defined, it falls back to the default scalar implementation, which divides each element of the vector by the scalar value.

Finally, the function returns a reference to the vector, allowing it to be used in a chain of operations.

