#include <stdio.h>
#include <termios.h>

static void cliPressAnyKeyTTY(void) {
    struct termios oldt, newt;

    tcgetattr(STDIN_FILENO, &oldt);
    newt = oldt;
    newt.c_lflag &= ~(ICANON | ECHO);
    tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, TCSANOW, &newt);

    printf("Press any key to continue...");
    getchar();

    tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, TCSANOW, &oldt);
}
```
This function uses the `termios` library to put the terminal in "press any key" mode. It first retrieves the current terminal settings using `tcgetattr`, then it modifies the settings to disable canonical input and echoing of input characters. It then sets the modified settings using `tcsetattr`.

The function then prints a message to the user and waits for the user to press any key using `getchar`.

Finally, the function restores the original terminal settings using `tcsetattr` with the `TCSANOW` option.

Note that this function assumes that the terminal is in canonical mode, which is the default mode for terminals. If the terminal is not in canonical mode, this function may not work correctly.

