column5:
```c
static void cliPressAnyKeyTTY(void) {
    // Get the current terminal settings
    struct termios oldt;
    tcgetattr(STDIN_FILENO, &oldt);

    // Set the terminal to "press any key" mode
    struct termios newt = oldt;
    newt.c_lflag &= ~ICANON;
    newt.c_cc[VMIN] = 0;
    newt.c_cc[VTIME] = 0;
    tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, TCSANOW, &newt);

    // Read a character from the terminal
    char c;
    read(STDIN_FILENO, &c, 1);

    // Restore the original terminal settings
    tcsetattr(STDIN_FILENO, TCSANOW, &oldt);
}
```
This function uses the `termios` structure to set the terminal to "press any key" mode, which allows the user to press any key to continue. The function then reads a character from the terminal using `read()`, and finally restores the original terminal settings using `tcsetattr()`.

Note that this function assumes that the terminal is in canonical mode, which is the default mode for terminals. If the terminal is in non-canonical mode, the function may not work correctly.

